<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TO LIST LARGER ISSUES ON BOURSE.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TO LIST LARGER ISSUES ON BOURSE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The aims of Hungary's planned new law to regulate the securities market include boosting trade on the Budapest Stock Exchange, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>According to the draft approved by the government on Thursday the securities in public offerings over 200 million forint face value must be offered for bourse listing, Finance Ministry Deputy State Secretary Agnes Balazs told a news conference on Friday.</p>
<p>The Parliament is expected to pass the planned package of financial laws in September.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
